---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { sourceRegistry } from "../data/sourceRegistry.js";
const groups = [...new Set(sourceRegistry.map((source) => source.category))].map((category) => ({ category, sources: sourceRegistry.filter((source) => source.category === category) }));
---
<Layout title="Sources & Assumptions | ShouldISpend" description="See the outside sources ShouldISpend uses for market costs, consumer rules, and category assumptions, plus how those sources relate to calculator verdicts.">
  <main class="sources-page">
    <div class="eyebrow">Sources & assumptions</div>
    <h1>Outside facts support the inputs. They do not decide the verdict.</h1>
    <p class="intro">ShouldISpend uses outside sources when a page relies on market-cost benchmarks, consumer rules, definitions, or other facts that do not come from the user's own numbers. The pressure framework itself is explained in the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
    <section>
      <h2>How sources are used</h2>
      <p>A source may support a cost range, a definition, or a rule used for context. It does not mean the source endorses ShouldISpend, and it does not turn a general calculator into personal financial, legal, medical, tax, or insurance advice.</p>
      <p>Source dates are tracked so assumptions can be reviewed when underlying figures change. Calculator pages should identify the relevant source when a specific outside figure materially affects the page.</p>
    </section>
    {groups.map((group) => (
      <section>
        <div class="eyebrow">{group.category}</div>
        <h2>{group.category} source set</h2>
        <div class="source-grid">
          {group.sources.map((source) => (
            <article class="source-card">
              <h3>{source.title}</h3>
              <p><strong>{source.publisher}</strong></p>
              <p>{source.supports}</p>
              <p class="verified">Verified for ShouldISpend: {source.verified}</p>
              <a href={source.url} rel="noopener noreferrer">Open source →</a>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
    <section>
      <h2>What a citation does not mean</h2>
      <p>National averages can differ from a local quote, insurance determination, school offer, or household budget. Use the cited figures as context, then replace them with the real numbers available for the decision whenever possible.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
<style>
.sources-page{width:92%;max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;padding:72px 0 40px}.eyebrow{color:var(--primary);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.7px;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:14px}h1{font-size:clamp(2.7rem,6vw,4.8rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:0 0 24px}.intro,p{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.04rem;line-height:1.8}.intro{max-width:850px}section{margin-top:64px}h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.5vw,2.5rem);margin:0 0 18px}.source-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(270px,1fr));gap:20px}.source-card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px;padding:24px}.source-card h3{font-size:1.2rem;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 12px}.source-card p{font-size:.96rem;margin:0 0 12px}.source-card .verified{font-size:.86rem}.source-card a{color:var(--primary);font-weight:800}@media(max-width:700px){.sources-page{padding-top:52px}.source-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
